course: dictionary
lesson: 11465
title: Words for moving forward
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Advancement is a noun, and it has a few related meanings. The clues are in the words around it. «Advancements in medicine have helped doctors save many lives.» Here advancements means improvements, things getting better over time.
explain: At work, advancement means moving up to a better job. «Nina hoped for advancement at the bank, so she worked late every evening.» Check it by swapping in promotion: «Nina hoped for promotion at the bank» still makes sense, so advancement means moving up.
explain: Advancement can also mean helping something move forward. «The advancement of science helps us understand the world.» Ask yourself: what is moving forward? Here it is science, so the word means that science is growing and improving.
fact: Advancement means progress or improvement in something, such as science or medicine.
fact: Advancement can mean moving up to a better job or position, which is also called promotion.
fact: Advancement can mean helping something move forward.
fact: «Advancements in technology» means new and better technology over time.
fact: A good check is to swap in improvement or promotion and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Advancements in medicine have helped doctors save many lives.» What does advancements mean here? | *Improvements that move things forward | Stories about old doctors | Long, boring lessons | Bad things that make people ill
exercise: «Nina hoped for advancement at the bank, so she worked late.» What does advancement mean here? | Leaving the bank forever | *Moving up to a better job | Counting money | Closing the bank early
exercise: «The advancement of science helps us understand the world.» What does advancement mean here? | Stopping science | Writing a science book | *Helping science move forward | Forgetting science
test: «Chances for advancement make a job more exciting.» Which word is closest in meaning to advancement here? | Mistake | Lost property | *Promotion | Silence
test: Which word is closest in meaning to advancement in «advancements in technology»? | Tiredness | Accidents | *Progress | Breaks
exam: Which sentence uses advancement to mean moving up at work? | The advancement of medicine saved many lives | Advancements in phones are fast | The advancement of science is slow | *She won advancement to team leader
